{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"Reproduced deterministically: a `git` wrapper that execs `sleep` for the target subcommand, with `_GIT_TIMEOUT` set to 1 s. Against a repo with `origin` configured and a valid HEAD, `has_remote` returned False for a slow `git remote`, and `resolve_ref(\"HEAD\", fetch=False)` raised SnapshotRefError \"cannot resolve ref 'HEAD'\" for a slow `git rev-parse`.\n\nRoot cause: `git_run` folded TimeoutExpired into a private rc-124 result, and `rev_parse`/`has_remote` read its empty stdout as \"no SHA\" / \"no remotes\".\n\nFix (Gerrit 3258): `git_run` -> `gitutil.run_git_bounded`; `has_remote` and `rev_parse` check `git_outcome.is_watchdog_timeout` and raise SnapshotError naming the operation and bound (not SnapshotRefError, so the attested materializer's `except SnapshotRefError` fallback does not swallow it). `_ensure_blobs_present` still skips silently on that error, keeping its best-effort contract. Tests: tests/unit/test_snapshot_git_watchdog_d33f.py (6; 4 failed before the fix). Lint and typecheck pass; 967 snapshot/delta-tree/workflow tests and 3083 tests referencing the snapshot module pass."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793696870223243001,"uuid":"9aca1df5-8bd0-42b1-a8c4-cafa2461cc5d"}